  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1200 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nWednesday night through Monday:\n\nThe stationary frontal boundary bringing the active pattern for\nthe start of the week is expected to gradually sag southward \nfor the second half of the week. While cannot completely rule \nout some lingering shower/storm chances for far southern \nportions of our CWA on Thursday, the better upper-level forcing \nwill gradually slide east as the upper-level low progresses into\nQuebec. By Friday, global models have the upper-level ridge \naxis build across the Upper Midwest allowing for surface high \npressure to build across the Great Lakes. Thus looking at a \nbrief break in PoPs for the end of the week along with near to \nslightly below normal temps.\n\nHowever, this quiet stretch will not last as a trough develops \nover the central CONUS and slides eastward through the weekend. \nGFS and ECMWF along with their ensemble members show a \ndeveloping surface low accompanying this upper-level wave. \nExpect this low to develop over the Plains for the start of the \nweekend and eventually trek eastward later Saturday into early \nSunday. Still plenty of uncertainty on timing and exact track of\nthe weekend activity, but still a strong and consistent of \nenough signal for increased shower and thunderstorm chances for \nsouthern WI during this time. \n\nWagner",
